% Status: Draft v0.5.1.
%   v0.5.1 follows two CTO clarifications on top of v0.5:
%     1. The first segment of the URA tail is the user-id, not the
%        agent-id. Projects are user-owned (a user is stable; the
%        agent the user uses is ephemeral). Ability ownership in
%        EasyNet ontology extends from `agent owns ability` to
%        `(user | agent | hub | resource) owns ability`.
%     2. The URA tail is not a single dot-flat string. It is
%        `<dot-id-part>/<slash-path-part>`. The id part denotes the
%        owner-and-project; the path part is the byte address inside
%        the project, slash-separated, mirroring filesystem layout.
%        A resource URA therefore directly addresses a public byte
%        stream — `index.html`, `style.css`, `assets/logo.png` —
%        not the project enclosing it.
%   The ability namespace stays at one ability per project (not one
%   per file). The ability accepts the path through args; the URA
%   form `<user>.<project>/<path>` is purely an addressing form, not
%   a per-file ability proliferation.
%
